  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#44306\", \"PowerToys#38837\", \"PowerToys#21850\"], \"answer\": \"This has been reported before. Keyboard Manager's Disable remap only matches the exact shortcut (Alt+Tab). If another key is held at the same time, the shortcut falls through to Windows and still works. The maintainers say this is by design, and a request to add a fallthrough option is tracked in PowerToys#21850 (PowerToys#38837 was closed as a duplicate of it). The only workaround is to add a separate Disable remap for each combination you want blocked, for example Alt+W+Tab. Keyboard Manager supports at most 2 modifiers plus 1 key, so you cannot cover every combination. Please add a thumbs-up or your use case to PowerToys#21850.\"}",
